    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Corbin Carroll** (77.56) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (76.91) headline our lineup as the premier plays. **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a favorable matchup against Clay Holmes, and despite a slight drag from Holmes\u2019s elite holding of runners, his high-tier base projection makes him an auto-start. **Tyler Soderstrom** receives a massive +16% park adjustment and a wind-aided boost, elevating him into must-start territory against Shane Baz. Meanwhile, **Trevor Story** (71.91) remains a high-floor play, leveraging a strong park factor and wind blowing out at his venue to provide significant secondary punch in the middle of our order.\n\nWe are hunting stolen bases and favorable matchups, which puts **James Wood** (63.92) and **Mickey Moniak** (66.49) in solid positions. While **Mickey Moniak** faces a formidable arm in Aaron Nola, he carries a heavy platoon advantage that mitigates the risk, even with Nola\u2019s ability to control the running game. The bench remains crowded, but **Cole Young** (52.21) was the toughest exclusion; while he benefits from a weak matchup against Anthony Kay, the optimizer favored the higher-order stability provided by our incumbents. We are slightly concerned by the volume of \"Lineup Pending\" tags, particularly for **Gabriel Moreno** and **Dalton Rushing**, whose efficiency scores could swing significantly if they are pushed down the lineup card later today. \n\nWe are keeping a close watch on **Vinnie Pasquantino** (55.60); while his score is bolstered by a strong platoon edge, he is facing Burch Smith, whose elite xERA (2.33) presents a genuine threat to our daily production. Despite the presence of high-upside bench options like **Austin Riley** and **Zach McKinstry**, the current efficiency model dictates that we maximize our exposure to the favorable matchups of **Josh Naylor** (68.04) and the rest of our starting core. Ensure that if any late lineup changes occur, we shift focus to maximize our stolen base potential, as the scarcity of that category remains the primary driver of our overall roster strategy for Ghost Ride the WHIP.",
